import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse('{"title":"Exec erases type annotations — signatures are typecheck-owned metadata","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Exec erases type annotations — signatures are typecheck-owned metadata","type":"adr","date":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z","status":"accepted","applies_to":"`host` (`handl-runtime`, `plugin-lib-handl`, `plugin-lib-stdlib`), `kit-prelude-lang`, `lib-loader`"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"handl/project/adrs/0151-exec-erases-type-annotations.md","filePath":"vendored/handl/project/adrs/0151-exec-erases-type-annotations.md"}'),a={name:`handl/project/adrs/0151-exec-erases-type-annotations.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="adr-0151-exec-erases-type-annotations-—-signatures-are-typecheck-owned-metadata" tabindex="-1">ADR-0151: Exec erases type annotations — signatures are typecheck-owned metadata <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-0151-exec-erases-type-annotations-—-signatures-are-typecheck-owned-metadata" aria-label="Permalink to “ADR-0151: Exec erases type annotations — signatures are typecheck-owned metadata”">​</a></h1><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to “Context”">​</a></h2><p>Module prep (<code>transform_export_to_object</code>) rewrites top-level <code>export name &lt;::|:=|:|=&gt; expr</code> declarations into an object literal the exec engine evaluates. It already erased two annotated forms — <code>export Name: Type</code> binds <code>null</code>, and <code>export f: Sig := body</code> binds the body — but two holes remained where <em>type expressions</em> still reached the evaluator:</p><ul><li><code>export Name := A ~[N]~&gt; B</code> — a signature binding whose RHS <code>dim_arrow</code> evaluates its source/target children to mint an Arrow descriptor record. Boundary children are not evaluable: the lib-cli port&#39;s <code>export Run := ([String]) ~[1]~&gt; Result&lt;Output, Spawn&gt;</code> crashed eval because <code>Result&lt;Output, Spawn&gt;</code> is a type-level generic application (a <code>dimension</code> node) whose former application is not a runtime arrow. Likewise <code>export Argv := (String, [String], ...) ~&gt; [String]</code> mints a closure whose <code>[T]</code> list-type params can never bind.</li><li><code>eval.type-annot</code> — the canonical eval scheme projected the annotation child, bound its <em>value</em> into the environment, then evaluated the subject. Any <code>x: T</code> inside executed code therefore evaluated <code>T</code> at runtime, which crashes on the same generic-application shapes.</li></ul><p>This is an Agda-style violation: annotations are static metadata owned by the typecheck engine; the exec/tree-walk engine must erase them, never evaluate them.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to “Decision”">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Signature exports erase to <code>null</code>.</strong> <code>is_signature_rhs(rhs)</code> detects a signature RHS — a depth-0 graded arrow <code>A ~[N]~&gt; B</code>, or an ungraded <code>(…, [T], …) ~&gt; B</code> whose parenthesized params contain a bare <code>[</code>/<code>{</code> element (a list/record type that <code>closure</code> can never bind; <code>x: [T]</code> annotations and <code>xs[i]</code> indexes don&#39;t count) — and module prep binds <code>null</code>, the same value type-only <code>export Name: Type</code> gets. <code>dim_arrow</code> never mints a callable, so no runtime behavior is lost; typecheck reads the raw AST and is unaffected.</li><li><strong>The mirror stays in lockstep.</strong> The transform is applied to every copy of export-to-object: <code>handl-runtime::module_prep</code>, the <code>plugin-lib-handl</code> bootstrap, the <code>plugin-lib-stdlib</code> loader, and lib-loader&#39;s <code>index.hnl</code> (<code>is_signature_rhs</code>/<code>type_only</code> mirror).</li><li><strong><code>eval.type-annot</code> evaluates the subject only.</strong> The canonical scheme in <code>kit-prelude-lang</code> no longer evaluates or binds the annotation child. <code>type.type-annot</code> still synthesizes the annotation for typechecking — only exec changed.</li></ol><p>Commits: <code>host</code> cc1b65fd, <code>kit-prelude-lang</code> 8987453, <code>lib-loader</code> 15c06c6a.</p><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to “Consequences”">​</a></h2><ul><li>Private top-level bindings keep evaluating — e.g. <code>read = (Int) ~[1]~&gt; Nat</code> is still consumed as a <code>handle</code> target, and <code>f ~[2]~&gt; g</code> inside do-blocks still mints the n-cell records <code>&gt;&gt;&gt;[k]</code> pastes on. Only <em>exported</em> signature RHSs erase.</li><li><strong>Caveat:</strong> top-level <code>export law := f ~[2]~&gt; g</code> cells also erase — the detector sees a depth-0 <code>~[</code> and cannot distinguish a morphism-cell from a signature arrow. Accepted as signature-metadata semantics: an exported <code>A ~[N]~&gt; B</code> cell was never callable anyway (<code>dim_arrow</code> mints a descriptor record, not a function). Revisit only if exported higher-cell expressions need runtime values.</li><li>The four export-transform mirrors must move together; a divergence is a loader-parity bug (lib-loader&#39;s <code>.hnl</code> copy is the self-hosting path).</li></ul>`,10)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};